{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CeyCF3phRPj6hFpZXCerj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have delivered the independent Critic framing as requested. Summary of what the artifact covers:\n\n- **Authoritative requirements**: decomposed the five request obligations (derive required inputs, resolve schools safely, normalize metrics, construct exact requests, surface planner-generated bad requests as failures) and anchored each to the pinned v0.3.0 registry, per-question schemas, `_index.json`, input catalog, and `rules.md`.\n- **Scope and compatibility boundaries**: contract ownership of policy, the static-closed vs release-derived vs open vocabulary split (OD-03), the identity error boundary (`bad_request` vs `unanswerable`), conditional `distance_km` materiality (O-8/G-4/CR-5), emitter-enforced filter rules (OD-07), and hard out-of-scope items.\n- **Initial hypotheses (H1–H9)**: kept explicitly provisional, each testable by a later current-state inspection.\n- **Required implementation and test evidence**: derivation logic, resolution path, metric normalization, schema-exact construction, error classification (including the negative test that a planner defect is not emitted as `Unsupported`), determinism, and golden-suite alignment.\n- **Failure modes and acceptance hazards**: led with the central hazard of masking the target defect as a refusal, plus materiality mis-gating, name-matching leakage, vocabulary misclassification, drift-prone shims, and conflated `bad_request` semantics.\n\nI flagged that the timestamped `request.md` copy was not returned with divergent content, so I relied on the mirrored request text and the pinned Definition Pack, and I made no pass/fail determination — that remains host-owned."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7553,"cache_read_input_tokens":65563,"cache_creati